Chapter: GpuMemLaunderPure

 Probe: the GPU command buffer has its own typed surface. gpu-mem-write
 and gpu-mem-read carry the Gpu.Memory effect row, so a function with a
 pure signature cannot compose a triangle through them. The effectful
 call cannot hide in a plain let (CDX2033) and the Gpu.Memory effect is
 not declared in the signature (CDX2031).

 This is the compile-time half of the window guard. The runtime half
 (cap-gpu-mem-denied) refuses a raw poke-32 into the window without the
 bit, but a refusal met at runtime is a silent -1 and a black screen.
 The row is what turns that into a diagnostic at the definition site,
 which is the same bargain gpu-out struck for the port window.

Section: Definitions

  scribble-cmd : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scribble-cmd (base) (val) =
   let w = gpu-mem-write base 0 val
   in gpu-mem-read base 0

  opening : Text = show (scribble-cmd 3187671040 1)

